BV155CA.YAG, optimized 26'boom
21.000 21.225 21.450 MHz
5 elements, inches
           1.045    0.875    0.500    0.438 
  0.000    2.500   78.250    3.250   62.625 
 48.000    2.625   66.130    3.250   64.875 
 96.000    2.500   66.250    3.250   63.875 
178.750    2.500   66.250    3.250   61.625 
306.000    2.500   66.250    3.250   55.000 

This element taper is that of the Hy-Gain 155BA or
155CA. Note that the .5" o.d. section is modeling
the taper swaging of the .875" o.d. element tubing,
and the length of the 0.5" section subtracts from
the overall 84" or 72" length of the first section
-- as does the modeling of the element clamp and
boom also, represented by the 1.045" first section.

This design was optimized for F/R over band > 20 dB,
and SWR over the band < 2:1, with a mid-band free-
space gain of 9.9 dBi. Torque compensator is 2.5" OD 
PVC, 39.625" long, mounted 12" behind Director 3, 
on flat metal plate with U-bolts. 
